Interoperability notes (formats only; no code from these projects is included):

  - The mapfile written by the data-rescue engine is compatible with GNU
    ddrescue's mapfile format. The backup image format is compatible with
    Partclone's image format 0002 and the LZ4 frame format.
  - The LZ4 block, LZO1X (including LZO-RLE) and Zstandard decompressors
    (core/src/decomp*.cpp, used for Btrfs and F2FS compression) are written
    from the published format descriptions (LZ4 block format, RFC 8878) and
    checked against the output of the reference compressors. No code of
    those projects is included.
  - Btrfs, XFS and F2FS are implemented from their public on-disk format
    documentation (btrfs wiki, "XFS Algorithms & Data Structures", the F2FS
    layout). Field layouts and constants were checked against the kernel's
    format headers; no kernel code is included (docs/provenance-btrfs-xfs.md).
  - LUKS1/LUKS2 (dm-crypt data layer) and BitLocker are implemented from the
    public on-disk format documentation. Test vectors under core/tests are
    outputs of public reference implementations (hashlib, cryptography,
    argon2-cffi) and carry no code.
